# Rust build artifacts
#
# `/target/` alone matches only the ROOT package's target directory. Before the
# crates were made workspace members, each sibling crate had its own target
# directory which this pattern did not cover, so `git add -A` offered 745
# build-artifact files for staging. `target/` (no leading slash) matches at any
# depth and covers the root plus every workspace member.
target/
Cargo.lock.bak
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo Fuzz
/fuzz/target/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/corpus/

# IDE & Editor files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.iml
.project
.settings/
.kilo/


# OS generated files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Environment and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Profiling and coverage
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Audio test dumps & temporary files
*.wav.tmp
*.pcm.tmp
*.raw.tmp

# Generated decode fixture corpus. `testdata/fixtures.toml` (the manifest) IS
# committed — it is the recorded expectation the smoke test checks against —
# but the encoded audio is not: 35 s of lossless stereo is several MB per file,
# and every GStreamer version bump would churn them for no reviewable benefit.
# Regenerate with `scripts/make_fixtures.sh`.
/testdata/fixtures/
